            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0908" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.48 Earthquake of 1931/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-02">April 2, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Your telegram filed April 1, 7 a.m. Marine Corps has ordered that Marines due
                    to leave Managua on the <hi rendition="#italic">Chaumont</hi> tomorrow be
                    retained <pb facs="0909" n="789" xml:id="pg789"/> in Nicaragua for the present.
                    This will not interfere with the program of reducing the Marines as specified by
                    June 1.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
